  FontSize->0.9 Inherited,ExpressionUUID->
  "5201ec88-48e8-47b0-bad0-10db8129ec23"],
 "\[LineSeparator]",
 "is the list of the names of the catalogue models that ",
 Cell[BoxData[
  TemplateBox[{
    Cell[
     TextData["SullivanModel"]], "paclet:ChernSimons/ref/SullivanModel", 
    "ChernSimons Package Symbol"},
   "PackageLink",
   BaseStyle->"InlineFormula"]], "InlineFormula",ExpressionUUID->
  "d36a7bd7-f1b5-466f-8fe4-c81dfed40dc3"],
 " gives.",
 "\n"
}], "Usage",ExpressionUUID->"3f0eff6c-962d-4ef5-b952-ef87d0c09bf6"],

Cell[TextData[{
 "A name that takes a parameter is used as ",
 StyleBox["name", "TI"],
 "[",
 StyleBox["k", "TI"],
 "]:"
}], "Notes",
 CellFrameLabels->{{Inherited, Inherited}, {Inherited, 
    Cell[
     TextData[{
      "26.09.30: Design review - the catalogue is a list of strings, and a \
name that takes a parameter is used with the parameter as its argument, as in \
\"Sphere\"[4], so the list itself holds names only and SullivanModel matches \
the parameter in the name. The names are the full English names of the \
spaces, as the naming rule of the paclet asks. The symbol is a global list \
and so carries the $ of a global parameter; no alternative name was recorded. \
Prior art: the Wolfram Language has no catalogue of spaces or of their \
rational models. The engine the verification suites load keeps the same nine \
names in its own list, and the suites compare the models of this catalogue \
with the engine's.", "\n\n", 
       Cell[
        BoxData[
         GridBox[{{
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Edit"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationButton"]]], 
            StyleBox[
             RowBox[{
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "LastAnnotator"]], "pavel"}], 
             "TextAnnotator"], 
            Cell[
             BoxData[
              ButtonBox[
               DynamicBox[
                FEPrivate`FrontEndResource[
                "DocumentationToolsStrings", "Delete"]], BaseStyle -> 
               "TextAnnotationRemoveButton"]]], ""}}, 
          GridBoxAlignment -> {
           "Columns" -> {Left, Left, Right, Right}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}, 
